      {
        "id": 13189,
        "name": "Pinecone3",
        "username": "Pinecone3",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pinecone3/{size}/2494_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-06-25T18:23:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Most of the evidence we currently have points to Progeny's creator being the ultimate villian of the Multiverse. &nbsp;My question is, who is working for him, or inadevertantly helping him, or hindering him? &nbsp;For example:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul>\n<li>Grand Warlord Voss certainly does not seem the type who wants to destroy the world, just to conquer it. &nbsp;However, in the wake of his reign of terror, the galaxy at large seems to have become much more chaotic. &nbsp;And Progeny feeds on Chaos.</li>\n<li>Apostate's motives and mission--as well as his connection to Fanatic--are still largely shrouded in mystery. &nbsp;Are the Host and the Cosmic entity in cohorts, or even possibly the same thing?</li>\n<li>The Dreamer is obviously interconnected with the shattering of the timelines in some capacity. &nbsp;The work of the Progenitor? &nbsp;Or a coincidence?</li>\n<li>Deadline seems to be actively opposing the coming of the Cosmic Entity. &nbsp;What does he know that we don't?</li>\n<li>Who are the voices that drove Infinitor insane? &nbsp;Is the Cosmic Entity involved?</li>\n<li>Where does the Wager Master fit in? &nbsp;Who made the \"wager that nothing would happen?\" &nbsp;Was it the Cosmic Entity? &nbsp;Is he now trying to reverse the fact that he wagered incorrectly?</li>\n</ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Personally, I really don't know what to make of all of this, but I'd like to hear other people's speculations on the issue.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:55.368Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
