        "raw": "<p>Most of the evidence we currently have points to Progeny&#39;s creator being the ultimate villian of the Multiverse. &nbsp;My question is, who is working for him, or inadevertantly helping him, or hindering him? &nbsp;For example:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Grand Warlord Voss certainly does not seem the type who wants to destroy the world, just to conquer it. &nbsp;However, in the wake of his reign of terror, the galaxy at large seems to have become much more chaotic. &nbsp;And Progeny feeds on Chaos.</li><li>Apostate&#39;s motives and mission--as well as his connection to Fanatic--are still largely shrouded in mystery. &nbsp;Are the Host and the Cosmic entity in cohorts, or even possibly the same thing?</li><li>The Dreamer is obviously interconnected with the shattering of the timelines in some capacity. &nbsp;The work of the Progenitor? &nbsp;Or a coincidence?</li><li>Deadline seems to be actively opposing the coming of the Cosmic Entity. &nbsp;What does he know that we don&#39;t?</li><li>Who are the voices that drove Infinitor insane? &nbsp;Is the Cosmic Entity involved?</li><li>Where does the Wager Master fit in? &nbsp;Who made the &quot;wager that nothing would happen?&quot; &nbsp;Was it the Cosmic Entity? &nbsp;Is he now trying to reverse the fact that he wagered incorrectly?</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Personally, I really don&#39;t know what to make of all of this, but I&#39;d like to hear other people&#39;s speculations on the issue.</p>",
